# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AIG230 Final Project — Group 7
#
# Anything listed here is deliberately kept OUT of the public GitHub repository
# that is submitted to the instructor.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Personal study material (not part of the submission) ------------------
# docs/study_guide is a private revision document written for exam preparation.
docs/study_guide/
docs/study_guide_build/

# Personal working notes written to answer my own questions about the
# project. Not part of the submission.
docs/notes/

# --- Datasets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw Tatoeba dumps are large and are reproducible with `make data`.
data/raw/
data/interim/
data/processed/
!data/**/.gitkeep
*.tsv
*.tsv.bz2
*.tar.bz2
*.csv.bz2
*.vec
*.vec.gz
*.bin

# --- Model artefacts --------------------------------------------------------
# Large binaries are attached to a GitHub Release instead of being committed.
artifacts/checkpoints/
artifacts/logs/
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
# The MUSE initialisation matrix is 32k x 300 float32 = 37 MB, and is
# regenerable from the .vec files with `make embeddings`.
*.npy
*.npz

# ...but the fitted tokenisers ARE tracked (~1 MB total). Inference needs the
# exact tokeniser a checkpoint was trained with, so keeping them in the repo
# means a downloaded checkpoint works immediately, with nothing to rebuild.
!artifacts/tokenizers/*.model
!artifacts/tokenizers/*.vocab
!artifacts/tokenizers/*.json
# ...but small, human-readable result files ARE tracked: the report is built
# from them, so they must be reviewable in the diff.
!artifacts/results/**/*.json
!artifacts/results/**/*.jsonl
!artifacts/results/**/*.csv
!artifacts/results/**/*.md

# --- Result bundles ---------------------------------------------------------
# results.zip is how artefacts come back from Colab; its contents are tracked
# individually under artifacts/results/ and reports/figures/, so the archive
# itself is redundant weight in the history.
results.zip

# --- Demonstration video ----------------------------------------------------
# The whole folder, not just known extensions: screen recorders drop project
# files, thumbnails and intermediate exports beside the finished video, and a
# multi-hundred-megabyte blob committed once stays in the history forever.
recording/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi
*.mkv
*.webm
*.m4v
!app/assets/*.gif

